[Music]  coming off of a heavy weather week here  in las vegas it's important to talk  about what to do if you get in a car  accident especially in the rain and  thanks to our sponsors for this next  segment eric palacios and associates we  have some helpful tips to keep in mind  eric thank you so much for joining us  today a lot to talk about we saw a  pretty intense weather day here in las  vegas this week which usually means we  see a lot of car accidents let's talk a  little bit about why we do see so many  accidents when it rains here in las  vegas  we did uh see a lot of accidents in the  past few days with rain and it's based  on on two factors one uh we get about  one-fifth of what the rest of the  country gets on average for  rainfall  and rain days uh in las vegas we average  about 20 days of rain per year  and that's not a lot so with that uh  comes more oil and debris that stays on  the roads for a longer period of time uh  so normally this is washed away by rain  so since we sometimes go months without  a rainstorm when it does rain the roads  are very slick and two because we don't  see much rain uh us as drivers sometimes  don't  change our driving habits when we are  driving in the rain so we will drive at  the same speed we won't slow down a bit  we won't add more room between the car  in front of us and our own car  so when there is a need to brake quickly  or to change our speed it leads to  accidents  and if we do get in a car accident what  tips or suggestions do you have as far  as what to do next  well even uh more importantly on days of  rain be careful when you get out of the  car a lot of times you'll see a chain  reaction accident because of the  conditions because it's harder to see  and the last thing you want to do is  step out of your car and then uh get hit  and be injured uh even worse so it's  important to take a breath make sure  that it's safe to get out of the vehicle  uh and then once you are safe then call  the police and they can come and help  you and investigate the accident  and then as we deal with the aftermath  of an accident i think a really big  question that we all have is should we  be the ones dealing directly with the  insurance companies  a lot of people think that it's a good  idea to talk to the insurance company on  your own but be aware that especially  the other drivers insurance company  their goal is to  not pay you or to pay you as little as  possible if it's their driver's fault  so they always record the conversations  they have to let you know they're  recording it but they still do and  they're trained to ask you questions  that will  elicit responses  that will later harm your case so it's  important if you're injured in an  accident to let an attorney handle these  conversations for you that way we can  protect your rights  and just real quick this is a little  confusing too to know when you're  supposed to call  versus 911 if you're in any sort of  trouble or accident  that's a great question uh 9-1-1 should  be only if you're injured in the  accident and  you need an ambulance  if you're not seriously injured if  you're okay but you still need an  officer to come and write a report and  investigate the accident then you can  call 3-1-1 it takes a little bit longer  but at least you're not clogging up the  emergency lines for something that's not  truly an emergency  well eric thank you so much for breaking  this all down for us we hope everyone  stays safe out there but just really  important to keep in mind if you're  driving especially in the rain so thank  you eric  thank you for having me  thank you to eric palacios and  associates for sponsoring this segment  give them a call at 702-444-7777

